---@field TotalImpact aws.cost_explorer.GenericDouble The cumulative dollar difference between the total actual spend and total expected spend. It is calculated as TotalActualSpend - TotalExpectedSpend.
---@field TotalActualSpend? aws.cost_explorer.NullableNonNegativeDouble The cumulative dollar amount that was actually spent during the anomaly.
---@field TotalExpectedSpend? aws.cost_explorer.NullableNonNegativeDouble The cumulative dollar amount that was expected to be spent during the anomaly. It is calculated using advanced machine learning models to determine the typical spending pattern based on historical data for a customer.
---@field TotalImpactPercentage? aws.cost_explorer.NullableNonNegativeDouble The cumulative percentage difference between the total actual spend and total expected spend. It is calculated as (TotalImpact / TotalExpectedSpend) * 100. When TotalExpectedSpend is zero, this field is omitted. Expected spend can be zero in situations such as when you start to use a service for the first time.

